{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And you shall observe this matter.</b> Now the plain sense of the verse says that He also commands for generations the things stated regarding this matter, yet we have not seen that our ancestors did so, and our Sages too did not command to do so. And it appears that from the verse's saying <b>לְחָק לְךָ</b> on its own and then returning to say <b>וּלְבָנֶיךָ</b>, it revealed the intent that it is along these lines — that the matters are not equal for Him and for His sons; for it should have said ״וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם אֶת הַדָּבָר הַזֶּה לְחָק עוֹלָם״, and from His saying ״לְחָק לְךָ וּלְבָנֶיךָ״ — this explains the intent that they are not equal in the matter. ״לְחָק לְךָ״ is everything stated regarding the matter; ״וּלְבָנֶיךָ עַד עוֹלָם״ is particulars from the matter. And the verse relied on what would come in other places — the particulars that apply for generations — and thereby excluded the particulars that do not apply for generations, which it did not mention there. And here too it clarified the matters by saying ״וְלֹא יִתֵּן הַמַּשְׁחִית לָבֹא אֶל בָּתֵּיכֶם לִנְגֹּף״ — that He would strike the Egyptians; and this thing is not found for generations."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:10.087158813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}